# Line-ending policy.
#
# Only the generated import graphs are pinned here. Everything else keeps whatever the checkout
# already does, so adding this file cannot renormalise the tree under a concurrent lane.
#
# Why the pin: `scripts/build-encounter-index.mjs`, `scripts/build-flavor-index.mjs` and the
# localization catalog generator all write their output with LF and then compare the file back
# byte-wise in `--check` mode. On a Windows clone with `core.autocrlf=true` the working-tree copy is
# checked out as CRLF, so a byte-identical file fails the freshness check as a stale import graph.
# Observed 2026-07-27 on master: `src/data/encounters/index.generated.js` differed from freshly
# generated content by exactly 93 bytes — the 93 CR characters — and matched exactly once line
# endings were normalised. `npm run check` died there (check:depth-program:contracts).
#
# `eol=lf` makes the checkout match what the generators write on every platform, so the byte-wise
# freshness comparison means what it says. The generators' `--check` paths additionally normalise
# line endings, so a tree that predates this file (or a tool that rewrote a copy with CRLF) still
# passes; this attribute stops the mismatch happening in the first place.
*.generated.js text eol=lf
src/data/frontierRegions/*.js text eol=lf

# Render-package seal inputs are also byte-pinned: `scripts/lib/releasePackaging.mjs` hashes the
# *working-tree* bytes of each pilot's motion bank (`sealMotionBankRef`) and of `pilots.json`
# (`sourceManifest`) into the package's `metadata.runtime`, and `check-bundle` recomputes them on
# CI. A Windows checkout holds those files as CRLF while the runner's Linux checkout holds LF, so
# a package sealed on Windows never matches the LF recomputation — observed 2026-10-01 as
# "runtime table does not match its compiled render.glb" on every branch that rebuilt packages on
# Windows. `eol=lf` makes the sealed bytes identical on every platform.
# The generated outputs are pinned too so their own bytes are stable if a future check hashes them.
assets/ships/motions/*.motion.json text eol=lf
assets/ships/render-packages/pilots.json text eol=lf
assets/ships/release/render-packages/**/render-package.json text eol=lf
src/render/renderPackageManifest.js text eol=lf
